{"choices":[{"message":{"content":"{\n  \"chapter_proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch1\",\n      \"title\": \"实体瘤中肠道微生物组与 ICI 疗效的临床关联证据\",\n      \"purpose\": \"系统评估不同实体瘤类型中肠道微生物特征（分类学、功能、动态变化）与 ICI 临床结局（ORR, PFS, OS）的观察性关联，明确证据强度、肿瘤特异性及外部干扰因素，避免将相关性误读为因果性或普适性生物标志物。\",\n      \"scope\": \"涵盖黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC、HCC 等主要实体瘤的回顾性与前瞻性队列研究；包括 16S rRNA、宏基因组及代谢组数据；区分基线特征与治疗期间动态变化；纳入阴性或矛盾结果以平衡证据；排除无微生物组数据的纯临床研究及非 ICI 疗法（如 CAR-T）研究。\",\n      \"substantive_threads\": [\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"跨癌种的‘响应者’微生物特征：一致性与异质性\",\n          \"argument\": \"尽管部分菌属（如 Akkermansia, Faecalibacterium）在黑色素瘤和 NSCLC 中反复被报道与疗效正相关，但跨癌种（如 HCC, CRC）及跨人群（地理、饮食）的通用生物标志物尚未确立，肿瘤微环境特异性显著影响微生物 - 疗效关联的方向与强度。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0002\",\n            \"P0014\",\n            \"P0023\",\n            \"P0090\",\n            \"P0121\",\n            \"P0298\",\n            \"P0349\",\n            \"P0478\",\n            \"P0534\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_notes\": \"需区分黑色素瘤（证据最强）与其他癌种（如 HCC 中 Akkermansia 作用不一致）；强调 P0478 和 P0534 指出的缺乏通用标志物现状。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"从分类学到功能：微生物组预测效能的分辨率升级\",\n          \"argument\": \"物种甚至菌株水平的分辨率（如特定 Faecalibacterium 菌株）及功能通路（如 SCFA 合成、氨基酸代谢）比属水平分类丰度具有更稳健的预测价值，解释了不同研究中分类学标志物不一致的原因。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0015\",\n            \"P0097\",\n            \"P0137\",\n            \"P0179\",\n            \"P0420\",\n            \"P0437\",\n            \"P0496\",\n            \"P0511\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_notes\": \"引用 P0015 和 P0437 关于菌株/基因水平优于物种水平的证据；P0496 提出的‘功能分散假说’解释标志物冲突。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"时间维度：基线状态与治疗期间动态稳定性\",\n          \"argument\": \"基线微生物组是主要预测窗口，但治疗期间的微生物稳定性（而非单一时间点丰度）及特定菌群的纵向轨迹（如 Akkermansia 动态增加）与长期生存更密切相关，提示动态监测优于单次快照。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0033\",\n            \"P0060\",\n            \"P0134\",\n            \"P0200\",\n            \"P0227\",\n            \"P0569\",\n            \"P0585\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_notes\": \"对比 P0060（辅助治疗基线预测）与 P0227/P0569（纵向稳定性/新辅助治疗）；注意 P0569 中早期 NSCLC 低多样性与好预后的反常关联。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"外部干扰与宿主背景：抗生素、PPI 及饮食的修饰作用\",\n          \"argument\": \"抗生素暴露（特别是 ICI 前近期使用）普遍与疗效降低相关，但存在癌种特异性例外（如 HCC）；PPI 及饮食模式（高纤维 vs 高脂）通过改变微生物组成间接调节疗效，且效应具有时间依赖性和人群特异性。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0033\",\n            \"P0123\",\n            \"P0129\",\n            \"P0155\",\n            \"P0236\",\n            \"P0339\",\n            \"P0517\",\n            \"P0545\",\n            \"P0547\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_notes\": \"强调 P0547 系统综述中黑色素瘤的阴性结果作为反例；P0275 关于 HCC 中抗生素无负面影响的特例；P0517 关于 PD-L1 高表达人群对抗生素更敏感的亚组分析。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"证据的边界：阴性结果、矛盾发现与方法学局限\",\n          \"argument\": \"相当比例的队列研究未复现微生物 - 疗效关联，或发现相反趋势（如某些菌在特定癌种中有害），这反映了方法学异质性（测序、队列）、混杂因素及生物学情境依赖性，而非单一‘真理’的缺失。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0019\",\n            \"P0275\",\n            \"P0301\",\n            \"P0327\",\n            \"P0478\",\n            \"P0565\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_notes\": \"必须纳入 P0019（NSCLC 肠道菌群无关联）、P0301/P0327（HCC/NSCLC 阴性结果）以纠正发表偏倚；引用 P0565 关于异质性的系统评价结论。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0083\",\n          \"reason\": \"主要聚焦 CAR-T 疗法，微生物组内容仅为背景提及，缺乏 ICI 特异性临床关联数据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0138\",\n          \"reason\": \"研究对象为过继性 T 细胞疗法（ACT/TILs），非 ICI 治疗，机制与人群不可比。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0256\",\n          \"reason\": \"仅报告 TNBC 临床疗效基线，无微生物组检测数据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0272\",\n          \"reason\": \"聚焦血液肿瘤及 CAR-T 联合 ICI，非实体瘤 ICI 单药或标准联合治疗背景。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0315\",\n          \"reason\": \"胸腺癌临床研究，未涉及微生物组分析。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0340\",\n          \"reason\": \"HCC 联合治疗疗效研究，无微生物组数据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0344\",\n          \"reason\": \"PD-L1 阴性/低 TMB 肿瘤 ICI 疗效研究，无微生物组数据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0404\",\n          \"reason\": \"甲状腺癌 ICI 疗效综述，无微生物组内容。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0410\",\n          \"reason\": \"超进展（HPD）临床研究，未检测微生物组。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0421\",\n          \"reason\": \"研究肌少症对 ICI 疗效影响，无微生物组数据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0426\",\n          \"reason\": \"转移部位对 ICI 疗效影响，无微生物组数据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0440\",\n          \"reason\": \"真实世界 ICI 使用模式及毒性，无微生物组分析。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0441\",\n          \"reason\": \"ICI 序贯化疗敏感性研究，无微生物组数据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0259\",\n          \"reason\": \"皮肤毒性观察研究，无微生物组数据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0395\",\n          \"reason\": \"病理反应作为替代标志物的讨论，无微生物组数据。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"supplement_requests\": [],\n      \"directed_reads\": [\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0585\",\n          \"reason\": \"JCOG2007 III 期试验的附属微生物组分析，需确认其具体的统计校正方法及亚组数据，以评估高级别证据强度。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0478\",\n          \"reason\": \"跨队列黑色素瘤研究，需详细提取其关于‘无通用标志物’的具体统计依据及队列间异质性来源分析。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"handle\": \"P0327\",\n          \"reason\": \"NSCLC 阴性结果研究，需确认其检测方法及队列特征，以作为平衡阳性发现的关键对照。\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screened_sources\": [\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0083\",\n      \"reason\": \"主要聚焦 CAR-T 疗法，微生物组内容仅为背景提及，缺乏 ICI 特异性临床关联数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0138\",\n      \"reason\": \"研究对象为过继性 T 细胞疗法（ACT/TILs），非 ICI 治疗，机制与人群不可比。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0256\",\n      \"reason\": \"仅报告 TNBC 临床疗效基线，无微生物组检测数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0272\",\n      \"reason\": \"聚焦血液肿瘤及 CAR-T 联合 ICI，非实体瘤 ICI 单药或标准联合治疗背景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0315\",\n      \"reason\": \"胸腺癌临床研究，未涉及微生物组分析。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0340\",\n      \"reason\": \"HCC 联合治疗疗效研究，无微生物组数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0344\",\n      \"reason\": \"PD-L1 阴性/低 TMB 肿瘤 ICI 疗效研究，无微生物组数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0404\",\n      \"reason\": \"甲状腺癌 ICI 疗效综述，无微生物组内容。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0410\",\n      \"reason\": \"超进展（HPD）临床研究，未检测微生物组。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0421\",\n      \"reason\": \"研究肌少症对 ICI 疗效影响，无微生物组数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0426\",\n      \"reason\": \"转移部位对 ICI 疗效影响，无微生物组数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0440\",\n      \"reason\": \"真实世界 ICI 使用模式及毒性，无微生物组分析。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0441\",\n      \"reason\": \"ICI 序贯化疗敏感性研究，无微生物组数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0259\",\n      \"reason\": \"皮肤毒性观察研究，无微生物组数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0395\",\n      \"reason\": \"病理反应作为替代标志物的讨论，无微生物组数据。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"The user wants a chapter proposal for \"Ch1: 实体瘤中肠道微生物组与 ICI 疗效的临床关联证据\" (Clinical Association Evidence between Gut Microbiome and ICI Efficacy in Solid Tumors).\nI need to structure this proposal based on the provided `source_routing` and `shared_level1_outline`.\nThe proposal must include:\n- `chapter_id`: \"Ch1\"\n- `title`: As provided or refined.\n- `purpose`: Refined purpose based on the routing evidence.\n- `scope`: Boundaries of the chapter.\n- `substantive_threads`: The core arguments/themes to be covered, ordered logically.\n- `excluded_source_handles`: Sources that are truly out of scope for this specific chapter (though most routed sources seem relevant to Ch1 based on the routing data, I need to check if any are better suited for other chapters or truly irrelevant).\n- `supplement_requests`: Any specific tool needs (though the prompt says \"source_routing has been fully preserved... only return chapter proposals... directed_reads\"). I should check if `directed_reads` is needed. The prompt says \"Return chapter_proposals... and screened_sources\". Wait, the prompt says \"Return JSON only\" and \"Return chapter_proposals... and screened_sources\". But the instruction also says \"Current task only responsible for the chapter specified... only return the proposal for that chapter\". I will follow the specific instruction for this turn: \"Return chapter_proposals (each with chapter_id, title, purpose, scope, optional excluded_source_handles, substantive_threads, supplement_requests, directed_reads) and screened_sources with non-use reasons.\"\n- `directed_reads`: Specific sources that need deep reading if not already covered.\n- `screened_sources`: Sources that were routed but deemed not usable for *this* chapter specifically (with reasons).\n\nKey constraints from the system prompt:\n- Do not write an intro/abstract/summary chapter.\n- Focus on substantive knowledge and analysis.\n- Do not simply list papers; synthesize arguments.\n- Preserve source handles.\n- Distinguish association vs causation.\n- Respect study conditions (tumor type, ICI type, etc.).\n- Do not overclaim (e.g., Phase III evidence where none exists).\n- Use the provided `source_routing` information.\n\nPlan for Ch1:\n1.  **Core Argument**: Establish the observational link between gut microbiome features (diversity, specific taxa, functional pathways) and ICI outcomes (ORR, PFS, OS) across solid tumors, while highlighting heterogeneity (tumor type, ICI regimen, geography).\n2.  **Themes**:\n    *   Global patterns: Diversity and \"Responder\" signatures (Akkermansia, Faecalibacterium, etc.).\n    *   Tumor-specific evidence: Melanoma (strongest), NSCLC, RCC, CRC, HCC, etc. (highlighting differences).\n    *   Resolution matters: Species/strain level vs. genus level, functional potential (metagenomics) vs. taxonomy (16S).\n    *   Dynamic changes: Baseline vs. longitudinal monitoring.\n    *   Confounding/Context: Antibiotics, PPIs, diet, host factors (age, BMI).\n    *   Negative/Null findings: Important to balance the narrative (e.g., some cohorts show no association).\n3.  **Sources**: I need to select from the `source_routing` list those assigned to \"Ch1\". Many sources are assigned to multiple chapters. I will list the handles relevant to Ch1 in the `substantive_threads` or implicitly rely on them. I need to explicitly list `excluded_source_handles` if any routed source is *not* suitable for Ch1 (e.g., if it's purely mechanistic without clinical association data, or purely about toxicity without efficacy data, though toxicity often correlates). Actually, the instruction says \"A source may support multiple chapters\". I should only exclude if it's genuinely out of scope for Ch1.\n    *   Looking at the routing, many sources are assigned to Ch1. I will keep them available.\n    *   Some sources might be better for Ch2 (mechanism) or Ch5 (intervention) but still have Ch1 relevance (clinical association). I will keep them in the pool but focus the *thread* on the clinical association aspect.\n    *   I need to identify sources that *only* talk about mechanism without clinical data (rare in this list, most reviews cover both).\n    *   I need to identify sources that are purely about toxicity (Ch6) without efficacy.\n    *   I need to identify sources that are purely about intervention (Ch5) without baseline association.\n    *   Actually, the instruction says \"Return chapter_proposals... and screened_sources with non-use reasons.\" I should check if any routed source is *not* useful for Ch1.\n    *   Most sources routed to Ch1 are useful. I will focus on organizing them.\n    *   I need to make sure I don't just list them but weave them into threads.\n\nRefining the Threads:\n1.  **Pan-cancer vs. Tumor-specific Signatures**: Compare the \"universal\" responders (e.g., *A. muciniphila*, *F. prausnitzii*) against tumor-specific findings (e.g., Melanoma vs. NSCLC vs. HCC). Use sources like P0002, P0014, P0023, P0090, P0121, P0298.\n2.  **Taxonomic Resolution & Functional Potential**: Discuss the shift from 16S to metagenomics/metatranscriptomics and the finding that function (e.g., SCFA pathways) might be more conserved than taxonomy. Use P0015, P0097, P0137, P0179, P0420, P0437.\n3.  **Temporal Dynamics**: Baseline vs. On-treatment changes. Stability as a predictor. Use P0033, P0060, P0134, P0200, P0227, P0569.\n4.  **Contextual Modifiers**: Antibiotics, PPIs, Diet, Host factors (Age, BMI). Use P0033, P0123, P0129, P0155, P0181, P0236, P0339, P0517, P0547.\n5.  **Inconsistencies & Null Results**: Acknowledge studies showing no association or contradictory findings to avoid overclaiming. Use P0019, P0275, P0301, P0327, P0478.\n\nExcluded Sources for Ch1:\n- Sources that are *purely* mechanistic (animal models only) without human clinical association data might be better for Ch2. However, many reviews mix them. I will check the `interpretation_limits`.\n- Sources purely about FMT intervention outcomes without baseline microbiome-efficacy correlation might be better for Ch5.\n- Sources purely about toxicity (irAEs) without efficacy data might be better for Ch6.\n- Let's look at the routing. Many sources have `chapter_ids` including Ch1. I will respect that. I will only exclude if I find a strong reason during planning (e.g., a source is purely about CAR-T or non-ICI therapy).\n- P0083 (CAR-T focus), P0138 (ACT/TILs focus), P0256 (TNBC clinical baseline only, no microbe), P0272 (CAR-T/HEMA), P0315 (Thymic carcinoma, no microbe), P0340 (HCC clinical baseline, no microbe), P0344 (PD-L1 neg, no microbe), P0404 (Thyroid, no microbe), P0410 (HPD, no microbe), P0421 (Sarcopenia, no microbe), P0426 (Metastatic location, no microbe), P0440 (Real world ICI usage, no microbe), P0441 (ICI sensitization, no microbe).\n- These sources were routed to Ch1 in the `source_routing` provided in the input (e.g., P0083 has `chapter_ids: [\"Ch1\", \"Ch2\"]`). Wait, the input `source_routing` shows many sources assigned to Ch1. I must follow the routing unless I find them genuinely out of scope.\n- However, the instruction says \"When an individual source is genuinely out of scope, name it in excluded_source_handles\".\n- P0083: Focuses on CAR-T, mentions microbiome as background. Might be weak for Ch1's core argument about ICI. I might exclude it or use it sparingly for contrast.\n- P0256, P0315, P0340, P0344, P0404, P0410, P0421, P0426, P0440, P0441: These seem to be clinical baseline studies *without* microbiome data, routed to Ch1 perhaps as \"context\". The prompt says \"Current task only responsible for chapter specified...\". If they don't have microbiome data, they are not evidence *for* the microbiome-efficacy association, but rather context for ICI efficacy heterogeneity. The chapter purpose is \"Systematically review observational associations...\". Sources without microbiome data don't fit the *evidence* requirement but might fit the *background*. However, the instruction says \"Do not write an intro chapter... substantive knowledge...\". I should prioritize sources with microbiome data. I will exclude those without microbiome data from the *substantive evidence* list but might keep them if they provide essential clinical context for the heterogeneity argument. Actually, better to exclude them from Ch1's *core evidence* to avoid dilution, as Ch1 is about \"Microbiome-Efficacy Association\". I will list them in `excluded_source_handles` with the reason \"No microbiome data\".\n- P0138 (ACT/TILs): Different therapy. Exclude.\n- P0272 (CAR-T/HEMA): Different therapy/tumor type. Exclude.\n\nLet's draft the JSON.\n\nStructure:\n- `chapter_id`: \"Ch1\"\n- `title`: \"实体瘤中肠道微生物组与 ICI 疗效的临床关联证据\"\n- `purpose`: ...\n- `scope`: ...\n- `substantive_threads`: List of themes with descriptions and key source handles.\n- `excluded_source_handles`: List of handles + reason.\n- `directed_reads`: Any specific needs.\n- `screened_sources`: (If any from the pool were screened out entirely, but here I'm working from the routed pool). The prompt asks for `screened_sources with non-use reasons`. I will put the excluded ones here.\n\nWait, I need to check the `source_routing` again. Some sources are assigned to Ch1 but might be better for Ch2/Ch5/Ch6. I can keep them in the pool for Ch1 if they have *some* Ch1 relevant data (e.g. a review that covers both association and mechanism). I will only exclude if they are *genuinely* out of scope (e.g. no microbiome data).\n\nLet's refine the `substantive_threads` to ensure they are argumentative, not just descriptive.\nThread 1: Consistency vs. Heterogeneity of Taxonomic Biomarkers.\nThread 2: Functional Potential > Taxonomy.\nThread 3: Temporal Dynamics (Baseline vs. Longitudinal).\nThread 4: External Modifiers (Abx, PPI, Diet).\nThread 5: Negative/Null Evidence (Crucial for balance).\n\nI will ensure the source handles cited in threads are from the `source_routing` list.\n\nOne more thing: The prompt says \"Return chapter_proposals... and screened_sources\". I need to make sure I output valid JSON.\n\nLet's check the excluded list again.\nP0083 (CAR-T), P0138 (ACT), P0256 (TNBC no microbe), P0272 (CAR-T), P0315 (Thymic no microbe), P0340 (HCC no microbe), P0344 (PD-L1 neg no microbe), P0404 (Thyroid no microbe), P0410 (HPD no microbe), P0421 (Sarcopenia no microbe), P0426 (Metastatic loc no microbe), P0440 (Real world no microbe), P0441 (Sensitization no microbe).\nThese are routed to Ch1 in the input but lack microbiome data. They are better excluded from a chapter specifically about \"Microbiome-Efficacy Association Evidence\". They might be useful for general ICI context but not for *this* chapter's specific evidence synthesis. I will exclude them to keep the chapter focused on microbiome evidence.\n\nAlso, P0259 (Skin toxicity no microbe), P0260 (Immunotoxicity review, mostly toxicity), P0395 (Path response surrogate). I will check if they have microbiome content. P0260 mentions microbiome in limits. P0395 is about path response. I will exclude those without direct microbiome-efficacy association data.\n\nOkay, ready to construct the JSON.","role":"assistant"},"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null}],"object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":101774,"completion_tokens":5811,"total_tokens":107585,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2975,"text_tokens":5811},"prompt_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":101774}},"created":1791137498,"system_fingerprint":null,"model":"qwen3.5-plus","id":"chatcmpl-86de5131-940c-983c-a3eb-a5680ee1df97"}